\par
\b 15. System Workflows by Scenario\b0\par
\b Scenario A: Model Development\b0\par
- Prepare and curate datasets.\par
- Train base model with staged freeze strategy.\par
- Expand class space and retrain V3 with selective oversampling.\par
- Validate with batch scripts and logs.\par
\par
\b Scenario B: Online Detection\b0\par
- Run ensemble detection on image or video stream.\par
- Trigger DINO only where required by policy.\par
- Apply post-filters and produce annotated output and logs.\par
\par
\b Scenario C: Temporal Monitoring\b0\par
- Detect per frame, track by ID, smooth with hold logic.\par
- Evaluate occupancy and obstruction conditions over time.\par
- Trigger alerts when duration thresholds are exceeded.\par
\par
\b Scenario D: RGB-D Safety Intelligence\b0\par
- Read synchronized RGB and depth.\par
- Convert detections to metric space.\par
- Validate physical plausibility.\par
- Persist trajectories and run anomaly geometry checks.\par
\par
\b 16. Performance and Reliability Considerations\b0\par
\b 16.1 Speed-Accuracy Tradeoff\b0\par
By keeping YOLO as primary detector and constraining DINO frequency and class scope, the system preserves practical throughput while improving weak-class recall.\par
\par
\b 16.2 False Positive Mitigation\b0\par
Mitigation stack includes class-specific confidence floors, context anchors, area limits, common-sense rules, and depth-based physical constraints.\par
\par
\b 16.3 Domain Shift Handling\b0\par
The framework explicitly acknowledges that validation AP does not guarantee identical deployment performance. Runtime fallbacks and rule layers are used to compensate for real-world scene shift.\par
\par
\b 17. Testing and Validation Strategy\b0\par
Current validation patterns in the repository include:\par
- Batch image testing for selected target classes.\par
- Comparative scripts for model version analysis.\par
- Temporal replay inspections with annotated outputs.\par
- RGB-D obstruction and zone checks against recorded sequences.\par
\par
Recommended additional maturity steps:\par
1. Standardized benchmark manifests for every use case.\par
2. Regression suites for key safety classes and anomaly events.\par
3. Automated schema checks for logs and DB outputs.\par
4. Consistent environment profile checks before run execution.\par
\par
\b 18. Deployment and Operations Guidance\b0\par
\b 18.1 Environment Profiles\b0\par
The project contains standard and hardware-specific requirements sets, including strict GPU paths for sensor-backed workflows.\par
\par
\b 18.2 Run Discipline\b0\par
For stable operations:\par
- Use consistent model path conventions.\par
- Keep output roots standardized per pipeline family.\par
- Include run tags and timestamps in artifacts.\par
- Archive configs together with outputs for reproducibility.\par
\par
\b 18.3 Operational Monitoring\b0\par
Monitor:\par
- per-class detection confidence distributions,\par
- alert frequency and persistence durations,\par
- ID churn rates,\par
- DINO invocation rate versus precision outcomes,\par
- depth validity rates in active scenes.\par
\par
\b 19. Risks, Constraints, and Technical Debt\b0\par
Key constraints currently visible:\par
- Multiple generations of scripts can reference differing path assumptions.\par
- Output directories are partially distributed across module-local and project-global roots.\par
- Some utilities remain environment-specific and may need portability hardening.\par
- Class mappings can drift unless governed centrally.\par
\par
Technical debt opportunities:\par
- Consolidate config into one central runtime config layer.\par
- Standardize model registry and output naming conventions.\par
- Add linted schema contracts for logs and DB tables.\par
- Introduce end-to-end integration tests for critical safety flows.\par
\par
\b 20. Roadmap Recommendations\b0\par
Near-term roadmap:\par
1. Canonicalize class dictionary and migration metadata.\par
2. Unify all run-time path configuration in a single source.\par
3. Add policy configuration files for thresholds and gating rules.\par
4. Build repeatable evaluation packs for corridor, ward, and OR scenes.\par
5. Expand anomaly ontology beyond blocked exit and spillage into workflow and compliance events.\par
\par
Mid-term roadmap:\par
1. Add service wrappers for deployment as streaming microservices.\par
2. Add event bus integration for real-time alerts and acknowledgements.\par
3. Add dashboard views over SQLite and CSV outputs.\par
4. Introduce model and prompt version tracking as first-class metadata.\par
\par
