\par
\b Object Plausibility\b0\par
- common_sense_filter.py: heuristic reality checks.\par
- rgbd_3d_filter.py: physical size and floor-aware depth filtering.\par
- hospital_object_dimensions_approx.yaml: metric priors for object dimensions.\par
\par
\b 22. Conclusion\b0\par
The Cognitive Recognition Framework is a multi-layer hospital vision system engineered for practical safety intelligence, not merely benchmark detection. Its strongest differentiator is the integration of model ensemble logic, context-aware fallback inference, temporal persistence, RGB-D geometric validation, and explicit anomaly-rule execution with auditable outputs.\par
\par
The project demonstrates a clear progression toward deployment-grade behavior: stronger reliability controls, richer 3D reasoning, and operational evidence generation. With continued consolidation of configuration and evaluation standards, the framework is well-positioned for production-oriented hospital safety monitoring use cases.\par
\par
\b End of Report\b0\par
